   },
   {
    "id": "rule",
    "type": "tex",
    "at": [
     0,
     -1.4
    ],
    "tex": "\\text{valid if } 0 \\le \\phi_q(i,j)-\\phi_k(i,j) \\le W-1",
    "hidden": true
   },
   {
    "id": "ex",
    "type": "tex",
    "at": [
     0,
     -2.5
    ],
    "tex": "i=11,\\ j=0:\\quad 11-0 = 11 \\;>\\; 3",
    "color": "red",
    "hidden": true
   },
   {
    "id": "jl",
    "type": "text",
    "at": [
     0,
     -3.6
    ],
    "text": "Jet-Long: close pairs keep their real positions. Far pairs use group numbers, floor(i/G), with G = ceil(12/4) = 3",
    "width": 14,
    "hidden": true
   }
  ]
 },
 "steps": [
  {
   "say": "Say the model was trained on 4 tokens, so the only query-to-key distances it has ever seen are 0 to 3. That's the green zone.",
   "board": [
    {
     "do": "set",
     "vars": {
      "d": 2
     }
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "say": "Now feed it 12 tokens. A query at position 11 looking at the key at position 0 is 11 apart, a distance the model has never seen, so attention breaks.",
   "board": [
    {
     "do": "show",
     "target": "ex"
    },
    {
     "do": "set",
     "vars": {
      "d": 11
     }
    },
    {
     "do": "color",
     "target": "dot",
     "color": "red"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "say": "A Pack recipe fixes this with two relabelling functions, phi q for the query and phi k for the key. It's valid if the relabelled distance always lands from 0 to W minus 1, for every pair.",
   "board": [
    {
     "do": "show",
     "target": "rule"
    },
    {
     "do": "highlight",
     "target": "safe"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "say": "Jet-Long is one example. Nearby pairs keep their real positions, and distant ones are squashed into groups of 3. So 11 becomes group 3 and 0 becomes group 0, a distance of 3, which is safely back in range.",
   "board": [
    {
     "do": "show",
     "target": "jl"
    },
    {
     "do": "transform",
     "target": "ex",
     "to": "\\lfloor 11/3\\rfloor - \\lfloor 0/3\\rfloor = 3 - 0 = 3 \\le 3"
    },
    {
     "do": "color",
     "target": "ex",
     "color": "green"
    },
    {
     "do": "set",
     "vars": {
      "d": 3
     }
    },
    {
     "do": "color",
     "target": "dot",
     "color": "green"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "say": "So the takeaway is that the definition just demands every distance gets pulled back into the trained window. The proposition proves Jet-Long always manages it.",
   "board": [
    {
     "do": "surround",
     "target": "rule"
    }
   ]
  }
 ],
 "title": "What a Pack recipe means"
}